ional behaviour checked by a cycle-accurate reference model before and after every edge, plus directed reads:\n- Level mode re-asserting pending while the source is high.\n- Edge mode latching a one-cycle pulse.\n- Detection winning over a same-edge W1C or acknowledge, in both modes.\n- Write data above bit 4 ignored on acknowledge.\n- Bits at N and above read as zero for N=8.\n- Mixed per-source modes.\n- A mode change while sources are held high.\n\nUnreachable by construction (justification, so they are not counted as dead code covered):\n1. unused_wdata = &{1'b0, wdata} is constant 0 in both instances. It exists only to mark ignored wdata bits.\n2. In dut_a (N=8), rdata[30:8] is constant 0. ENABLE, MODE and PENDING fill only rdata[7:0], and the CLAIM word drives only bit 31 and bits 4:0.\n3. In dut_a, irq_id[4:3] is constant 0, because the highest id is 7.\n4. In dut_b (N=32), the out-of-range acknowledge condition ({27'd0,wdata[4:0]} < N being false) cannot occur, because every 5-bit id is below 32. dut_a exercises that condition instead.\n\nThe loop variable i is an implementation detail of the priority encoder. Its toggle points, if a tool counts them, are not a design requirement."}], "files": [{"path": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv: coverage-closing self-checking testbench for irq_ctrl.v", "summary": "Extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1] to verify the approved RTL [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1] for [requirement:req-1e26d9c190].\n\nStructure:\n- Two instances of the RTL share one stimulus stream: dut_a with N=8 (the configuration of the approved testbench) and dut_b with N=32 (so every register, rdata and irq_id bit can toggle).\n- A cycle-accurate reference model checks rdata, irq and irq_id of both instances 1 ns before and 1 ns after every rising edge.\n- Directed register reads with fixed expected values are added at key points.\n- Stimulus runs in phases: res